<Layout title="Track Record — Apoorva Mehta, MD, MBA">
	<h1>Track Record</h1>
	<p>
		Three ventures, each one started before I'd finished training —
		because I wanted to see healthcare built differently, not just
		delivered.
	</p>
	<p>
		I co-founded <strong>ChartR</strong>, a company building long-horizon
		reinforcement learning environments for healthcare, alongside
		operational and applied AI within enterprise healthcare. The RL
		environment work is the harder, more distinctive half — few people
		building in that space also have a clinical background, which is
		exactly the gap ChartR was built to close. It's no longer active, but
		it's where I learned how hard it is to build AI that actually
		survives contact with a hospital.
	</p>
	<p>
		Before that, as a fellow at <strong>Rock Health Capital</strong>, I
		evaluated hundreds of early-stage digital health startups — commercial,
		technical, and clinical diligence — with end-to-end involvement on
		investments including Vitalize and HealthMC.
	</p>
	<p>
		And earlier, at <strong>SkinCheck</strong>, I helped grow a digital
		dermatology platform to 100,000+ downloads and 6,500 monthly active
		users, shaped its health-plan partnership strategy, and helped raise
		its pre-seed round.
	</p>
</Layout>
